& [CampaignInput] identifies one immutable source and build environment
  + [source_revision] is an invocation argument defaulting to HEAD
  + [source_commit] is the exact resolved commit object
  + [source_tree] is the exact tree bound by source_commit
  + [source_archive_sha256] binds the Git archive used for both source roots
  + [cargo_lock_sha256] binds dependency resolution
  + [toolchain_identity] records readable rustc version commit date release Cargo version host triple and LLVM version plus the full rustc verbose digest
  + [target_package] is cantor_field_cycle
  + [target_binary] is cantor_field_cycle.exe
  = must: fail unless source_revision resolves to one commit and required tools and files exist

& [BuildControls] defines the closed local profile
  + [cargo_command] is cargo build --release -p cantor_field_cycle --locked --offline
  + [SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH] is the exact source commit timestamp
  + [CARGO_INCREMENTAL] is 0
  + [RUSTFLAGS] is -C link-arg=/Brepro
  + [source_root_count] is 2
  + [target_root_count] is 2
  = must: extract the same archive into two distinct source roots
  = must: build each source root into its own initially absent target root
  = must: restore inherited environment values after the campaign
  - never: download dependencies mutate the source revision or reuse a target root

& [ArtifactComparison] is exact
  + [artifact_bytes] is the executable byte length
  + [artifact_sha256] is lowercase SHA-256
  + [byte_equal] is an exact byte-for-byte comparison
  = must: require equal lengths equal SHA-256 values and byte_equal true
  - never: accept timestamp metadata similarity or functional similarity as byte identity

& [BehaviorPreservation] is effect-free executable inspection
  + both executables must emit byte-identical contract output
  + both executables must emit the same sixty-four-character lowercase field digest for the retained attention_cycle_field fixture
  + both executables must successfully verify retained positive control and hostile-boundary reports
  + [provider_request_count] is 0
  + [external_effects] is none_except_local_temporary_build_files
  - never: invoke run control-run or any command that contacts a provider

& [Receipt] is deterministic evidence
  + [profile] is cantor-field-attention-reproducible-windows-build/0.1
  + [result] is passed only after every source build artifact and behavior gate passes
  + [stable_fields] include source identities tool identities build controls artifact identity behavior digests verification counts and claim boundary
  + [temporary_paths] are omitted
  + [receipt_output] is UTF-8 JSON on standard output
  = must: serialize stable object keys and arrays in one declared order
  = must: emit no positive receipt after a failed gate

& [CleanupBoundary] is fail-closed
  + all campaign files live below the repository target directory in one uniquely named campaign root
  + recursive cleanup is permitted only after the resolved campaign path is proven to be a direct child with the declared name prefix
  + explicit diagnostic retention may preserve the validated campaign root
  - never: recursively delete the repository root target root user profile drive root or an unresolved path

& [ProgramExecutionFlow] is closed
  + [F0 Resolve] records repository commit tree epoch lock and toolchain identities
  + [F1 Archive] creates one exact Git archive and hashes it
  + [F2 Isolate] extracts the archive into source-a and source-b and allocates distinct target roots
  + [F3 Build] applies the closed environment and command separately in each source root
  + [F4 Compare] requires exact executable identity
  + [F5 Inspect] compares contract and field-digest outputs and verifies three retained report classes with both executables
  + [F6 Emit] writes one deterministic receipt to standard output
  + [F7 Clean] safely removes the campaign root unless retention was explicitly requested
  + [failure] is nonzero exit with no passed receipt

& [AcceptanceCriteria] is measurable
  + [FARW-001] preserved source bytes hash manifest exploded specification justification and signature verify
  + [FARW-002] two source roots originate from one hashed archive of one exact commit
  + [FARW-003] both initially clean target roots build release cantor_field_cycle with locked offline dependencies and exact controls
  + [FARW-004] executables have equal bytes SHA-256 and byte length
  + [FARW-005] contract outputs and field digests are exactly equal
  + [FARW-006] both executables verify positive control and hostile retained reports for six successful verifier invocations
  + [FARW-007] receipt is deterministic omits temporary paths and states the local-only claim boundary
  + [FARW-008] default cleanup removes only a validated campaign root and retained mode reports retention without broad deletion
  + [FARW-009] existing focused and workspace verification remain green

& [AuthorityBoundary] is reversible experimental build-proof authority
  + [permits] is one PowerShell proof tool temporary files below target local compilation executable inspection deterministic receipt documentation and defect repair
  + [excludes] is inference provider access llama.cpp modification runtime semantic change CLI semantic change report mutation deployment installation ACL change production signing and P1 authorization
  + [nonclaim] is local byte equality does not establish cross-host reproducibility production supply-chain trust semantic truth or historical h8 provenance

